{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>There shall not be found in you one who passes his son.</b> The [phrase] 'there shall not be found' was [written] because even today there are among us many nations, fire-worshippers." "<b>A diviner of divinations.</b> It is possible that it is a noun of totality and its meaning is: those who decree fate, who say 'thus it will certainly be,' and so they decree. Close to it is 'divination on the lips of a king' (Proverbs 16:10). And the specific [forms] are מעונן, מנחש, מכשף. It is also possible that it is a specific noun, referring to astrologers, and the meaning of 'divinations' is that there are [divinations] in the judgments of the stars, called primary and secondary." "<b>An observer of clouds and a serpent-charmer.</b> I have explained them." "<b>And a sorcerer.</b> Likewise."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "Resolved ע״‎ג as על כן ('therefore/therefore was'), reading the line as explaining why the passive formulation was used; alternatively ע״ג may abbreviate עדות גדולה or similar.", 1 "Read חותכי משפט (construct plural) for what appears to be singular חותך משפט in the source; the plural sense is required by the surrounding plural participles."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:23:59.120650288Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}